  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "LaLxTOBD91agSjmrLwq+/fQXZ1M=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:00.079Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "x402 defines a **batch settlement** scheme (EVM-based) enabling high-volume, batched onchain redemption of micropayments.\n\n**Problem it solves:** individually settling sub-cent payments onchain would cost more in gas than the payment is worth. Batching amortizes settlement cost across many payments, which is what makes granular usage-based pricing (per API call, per query) economically viable.\n\n**Pattern:** accept many small offchain-verified payments, redeem them onchain in aggregate \u2014 the same accumulate-then-settle shape as payment channels and rollups.\n\nSource: x402 docs introduction (https://docs.x402.org/introduction).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:00.079Z"
    }
  },
